Consider the following recursive binary search method for a sorted array:

```java
public static int binarySearch(int[] arr, int target, int low, int high) {
    if (low > high) {
        return -1;
    }
    int mid = (low + high) / 2;
    if (arr[mid] == target) {
        return mid;
    } else if (arr[mid] > target) {
        return binarySearch(arr, target, low, mid - 1);
    } else {
        return binarySearch(arr, target, mid + 1, high);
    }
}
```

Given `arr = {5, 12, 18, 23, 30, 42, 50}` and the call `binarySearch(arr, 18, 0, 6)`, what are the values of `low`, `high`, and `mid` in the **first recursive call** (the call made after the initial call)?

(A) low = 0, high = 2, mid = 1
(B) low = 0, high = 3, mid = 1
(C) low = 3, high = 6, mid = 4
(D) low = 1, high = 2, mid = 1
